# Workload — PRNG-only baseline, drawing the same 1.2e8 doubles as orient3d.dl.
#
# Added in response to a review finding (I1): the orient3d and tritri timed
# regions start the clock before generation, so the PRNG draws are inside the
# measured time and that was not disclosed. This workload isolates the
# generation cost by drawing the *same* doubles in the *same* order as
# orient3d.dl — four sample points (12 doubles) per iteration, 1e7
# iterations — and doing nothing else in the timed region, so its median can
# be subtracted from orient3d's to estimate the determinant-only share.

import common.dl

function the quadruple count:
    replacement:
        10000000 as a 64 bit integer

reseed with 88172645463325252

set started to the clock milliseconds
set index to 0 as a 64 bit integer
loop while index < the quadruple count:
    set pa to the next random sample point
    set pb to the next random sample point
    set pc to the next random sample point
    set pd to the next random sample point
    set index to index + 1
set finished to the clock milliseconds

print real the input checksum
print integer the generator state
print integer (finished - started)
